---
/*
  BeforeAfter.astro — Before/After comparison for the landing page.

  Shows RFC 959 Section 3.1.1 plaintext side-by-side with the Pretty Docs
  formatted version, demonstrating the core value proposition. The "Before"
  card renders actual RFC text in Courier New; the "After" card shows the
  same content reformatted with data type icons (A=ASCII, I=Image, E=EBCDIC).

  No props — all content is static.
*/
---

<section class="before-after">
  <div class="before-after-inner">
    <div class="before-after-header">
      <h2 class="before-after-heading">Same content. Radically different experience.</h2>
      <p class="before-after-subtitle">
        RFC 959 was written in 1985. We think it deserves better than monospaced plaintext.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="comparison-grid">
      {/* Before card */}
      <div class="comparison-card card-before">
        <div class="card-header card-header-before">
          <div class="card-label">
            <div class="dot dot-red"></div>
            <span class="label-text label-text-before">Before &mdash; RFC 959</span>
          </div>
          <span class="url-hint url-hint-before">w3.org/Protocols/rfc959</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rfc-text">3.1.1.  DATA TYPES

      3.1.1.1.  ASCII TYPE

         This is the default type and must be accepted by all FTP
         implementations.  It is intended primarily for the
         transfer of text files, except when both hosts would
         find the EBCDIC type more convenient.

         The sender converts the data from an internal character
         representation to the standard 8-bit NVT-ASCII
         representation (see the Telnet specification).  The
         receiver will convert the data from the standard form to
         his own internal form.

         In accordance with the NVT standard, the &lt;CRLF&gt;
         sequence should be used where necessary to denote the
         end of a line of text.  (See the discussion of file
         structure at the end of the Section on Data
         Representation and Storage.)

      3.1.1.3.  IMAGE TYPE

         The data are sent as contiguous bits which, for
         transfer, are packed into the 8-bit transfer bytes.
         The receiving site must store the data as contiguous
         bits.  The structure of the storage system might
         necessitate the padding of the file (or of each record,
         for a record-structured file) to some convenient
         boundary (byte, word or block).  This padding, which
         must be all zeros, may occur only at the end of the
         file (or at the end of each record) and there must be a
         way of identifying the padding bits so that they may be
         stripped off if the file is retrieved.</div>
      </div>

      {/* After card */}
      <div class="comparison-card card-after">
        <div class="card-header card-header-after">
          <div class="card-label">
            <div class="dot dot-blue"></div>
            <span class="label-text label-text-after">After &mdash; Pretty Docs</span>
          </div>
          <span class="url-hint url-hint-after">prettydocs.dev</span>
        </div>
        <div class="after-body">
          <h3 class="after-title">Data Types</h3>
          <p class="after-description">
            FTP supports four data types that determine how file contents are
            interpreted during transfer. The type you choose depends on what
            you're sending and who's receiving it.
          </p>
          <div class="type-list">
            <div class="type-row">
              <div class="type-icon type-icon-brand">
                <span>A</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="type-name">ASCII</p>
                <p class="type-desc">Default type. Text files converted to 8-bit NVT-ASCII. Lines end with CRLF.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="type-row">
              <div class="type-icon type-icon-brand">
                <span>I</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="type-name">Image (Binary)</p>
                <p class="type-desc">Raw contiguous bits, packed into 8-bit bytes. No conversion. Use for non-text files.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="type-row">
              <div class="type-icon type-icon-muted">
                <span>E</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="type-name type-name-muted">EBCDIC</p>
                <p class="type-desc type-desc-muted">For mainframe-to-mainframe transfers. Rarely used today.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* =============================================
     Before/After comparison section
     ============================================= */

  .before-after {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--surface-200);
    background: var(--page-bg);
  }

  .before-after-inner {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 80px 24px;
  }

  /* --- Header --- */
  .before-after-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .before-after-heading {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--surface-900);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .before-after-subtitle {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--surface-500);
  }

  /* --- Grid --- */
  .comparison-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .comparison-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* --- Shared card styles --- */
  .comparison-card {
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease-out, box-shadow 0.3s ease-out;
  }

  /* --- Card headers --- */
  .card-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 12px 20px;
  }

  .card-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .dot {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .dot-red {
    background: #f87171;
  }

  .dot-blue {
    background: #5c7cfa;
  }

  .label-text {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .label-text-before {
    color: var(--surface-500);
  }

  .label-text-after {
    color: #4c6ef5;
  }

  .url-hint {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .url-hint-before {
    color: #ced4da;
  }

  .url-hint-after {
    color: #748ffc;
  }

  /* --- Before card --- */
  .card-before {
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-200);
  }

  .card-header-before {
    background: var(--surface-100);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--surface-200);
  }

  .rfc-text {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #495057;
    background: #f8f9fa;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-wrap: break-word;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  /* --- After card --- */
  .card-after {
    border: 1px solid #bac8ff;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px #dbe4ff;
  }

  .card-header-after {
    background: #f0f4ff;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dbe4ff;
  }

  .after-body {
    padding: 24px;
  }

  .after-title {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--surface-900);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .after-description {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--surface-700);
    line-height: 1.625;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  /* --- Type list (A / I / E rows) --- */
  .type-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .type-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .type-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .type-icon span {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .type-icon-brand {
    background: #f0f4ff;
  }

  .type-icon-brand span {
    color: #4c6ef5;
  }

  .type-icon-muted {
    background: var(--surface-50);
  }

  .type-icon-muted span {
    color: #ced4da;
  }

  .type-name {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--surface-900);
  }

  .type-name-muted {
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .type-desc {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--surface-500);
    line-height: 1.625;
  }

  .type-desc-muted {
    color: #ced4da;
  }

  /* =============================================
     Dark mode
     ============================================= */

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .before-after {
    border-top-color: #2e3150;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .before-after-subtitle {
    color: #c8cad8;
  }

  /* Before card — dark */
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .card-before {
    border-color: #2e3150;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .card-header-before {
    background: #1f2133;
    border-bottom-color: #2e3150;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .label-text-before {
    color: #c8cad8;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .url-hint-before {
    color: rgba(200, 202, 216, 0.5);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .rfc-text {
    color: #c8cad8;
    background: #1a1b26;
  }

  /* After card — dark */
  :root[data-theme='dark'] .card-after {
    border-color: rgba(76, 110, 245, 0.3);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(76, 110, 245, 0.1);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .card-header-after {
    background: rgba(76, 110, 245, 0.08);
    border-bottom-color: rgba(76, 110, 245, 0.15);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .label-text-after {
    color: #748ffc;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .url-hint-after {
    color: #5c7cfa;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .after-body {
    background: #1f2133;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .after-description {
    color: #c8cad8;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .type-icon-brand {
    background: rgba(76, 110, 245, 0.12);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .type-icon-brand span {
    color: #748ffc;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .type-icon-muted {
    background: #252740;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .type-icon-muted span {
    color: rgba(200, 202, 216, 0.5);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .type-desc {
    color: rgba(200, 202, 216, 0.7);
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .type-desc-muted {
    color: rgba(200, 202, 216, 0.4);
  }
</style>
